  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Crazy Eights. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Crazy Eights is a popular shedding card game, especially beloved by children. The objective is simple: be the first player to discard all your cards. Players take turns playing cards to a central discard pile, matching either the rank or suit of the top card. The eponymous "crazy" 8s are wild cards that can be played on anything and allow the player to change the suit.',
    objective: 'Be the first player to empty your hand by matching color, number, or action cards.',
    gameplay: 'Players play cards matching the current color or value, use action cards to change direction or color, and may stack same-color cards after a Taki card. The game resembles Uno but has its own deck and rules.',
    keyRules: [
      'Players match color, number, or legal action.',
      'A Taki card lets a player play multiple cards of the same color.',
      'First player to empty hand wins the hand.',
    ],
